Research Integrity Ledger
=========================

Integrity ledger for research artifacts. The system does not store the data itself,
but rather its digital fingerprint: it receives the SHA-256 hash of a document, seals
this hash into a cryptographically chained block, and any subsequent tampering is
detectable by comparing the current hash with the registered one.

Context
-------

This project originated from research in computer science applied to personalized
medicine, hence the need for an auditable record to ensure that research data would
not be altered after collection.

It is a learning proof-of-concept based on tutorials about building a blockchain in
Python, generalized into a domain-agnostic integrity ledger. It is not production
software; a real-world ledger would use a permissioned framework like Hyperledger Fabric.

Tutorial links:
https://adilmoujahid.com/posts/2018/03/intro-blockchain-bitcoin-python/
https://medium.com/@vanflymen/learn-blockchains-by-building-one-117428612f46

Quick Start
-----------

* pip install flask requests
* python ledger.py
* python ledger.py --port 5001

A bootstrap API key is printed to the terminal on the first run, SAVE IT!

